            "text": "What is MDF?",
            "heading_tag": "h1"
          }
        },
        "richtext_YdU4bm": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>MDF is a wood panel made of pine trees and their branches &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Special adhesives are added the mixture is pressed & heated &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The boards are then cut to the required sizes &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>MDF surface is completely smooth, its colors do not change over time &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The wood is then cracked and chopped &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>In the next stage the plates are formed and compressed &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Afterward, the outer layer coating is pressed &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>We import raw material from the E.U. to endure high quality&nbsp;</p>"
          }
        }
      },
